From: {{ $json.from && $json.from.text ? $json.from.text : "unknown" }}
Subject: {{ $json.subject || "(no subject)" }}
Body:
{{ $json.text && $json.text.trim().length ? $json.text : ($json.textAsHtml || $json.html || "(no body available)") }}

{{ $json.hasPendingProposal ? ("PENDING PROPOSAL CONTEXT: In a previous email on this thread, the following meeting time slots were already proposed to this sender: " + $json.pendingSlotsText + ". Check carefully whether THIS reply clearly confirms ONE of these specific slots.") : "" }}

STEP 1 -- CONFIRMATION CHECK: {{ $json.hasPendingProposal ? "Determine whether this reply clearly confirms one of the previously proposed slots listed above. If yes, set isConfirmingProposal to true and set confirmedSlotIndex to the zero-based index of the confirmed slot in that list (0 for the first slot listed, 1 for the second, etc). If the reply does not clearly confirm one specific slot from that list (for example if it declines, asks a question, or proposes a different time instead), set isConfirmingProposal to false and confirmedSlotIndex to -1." : "There is no pending proposal on this thread. Always set isConfirmingProposal to false and confirmedSlotIndex to -1." }}

STEP 2 -- CLASSIFY: If isConfirmingProposal is false, determine whether this email is a genuine, active request from a person asking to schedule an appointment, meeting, or call (this includes proposing a different time than one previously offered). Set isAppointmentRequest to true only for that case. Set it to false for automated calendar system notifications (invitation accepted/declined/updated, reminders), newsletters, webinar or event announcements, receipts, and any email that is not itself asking to schedule time with the recipient. If isConfirmingProposal is true, set isAppointmentRequest to false.

STEP 3 -- TIMEFRAME (only when isAppointmentRequest is true; otherwise use the empty defaults): requestedTimeframeHint is a short phrase quoting the preferred timeframe, or an empty string. preferredStartDate and preferredEndDate are the first and last acceptable days as YYYY-MM-DD, resolving relative expressions such as "next week" or "Friday" against today's date; use empty strings if no timeframe is given. preferredPartOfDay is "morning", "afternoon" or "any". durationMinutes is the requested meeting length in minutes, or 0 if not stated.

STEP 4 -- DRAFT:
- If isConfirmingProposal is true: write a short, warm reply in draftReply that confirms the specific agreed time. Do not say the meeting is already in the calendar and do not mention a calendar invitation. Reply in the same language as the original email. Sign off as {{ $json.senderName.split(" ")[0] }}.
- Else if isAppointmentRequest is false: first decide needsReply. needsReply is true only when a person expects an answer from the recipient (a question, a request, a personal invitation, something to confirm). It is false for newsletters, notifications, receipts, automated or bulk messages, messages where the recipient is only in copy with nothing asked, and short closings such as thanks or acknowledgements. If needsReply is false, set draftReply to an empty string. Otherwise write a complete, natural, ready-to-send reply in draftReply. Address the actual content of the email specifically -- do not write a generic acknowledgment. Reply in the same language the original email was written in. Follow the sender-specific instructions above if any are given. Sign off as {{ $json.senderName.split(" ")[0] }}.
- Else (a brand new appointment request with no confirmed slot yet): set draftReply to an empty string -- a later step drafts that reply once calendar availability is known.

STEP 5 -- EARLIER ITEMS: set refersToEarlier to true when the email asks about, or refers to, something the sender sent before: a document, file, attachment, link or earlier email (for example "did you read the document I sent you?" or "as per the file attached last week"). Then set referenceDescription to a short phrase naming it, and referenceKeywords to 1-5 distinctive words likely to appear in its file name or in the subject of the email that carried it. Otherwise set refersToEarlier to false, referenceDescription to an empty string and referenceKeywords to an empty list.

Respond with ONLY the JSON object matching the required schema. No explanation, no markdown code fences, no text before or after the JSON.

